(1146890, 142238, 31865, '<td valign="top">this sign is scary.  i like the REPENT!!! feel of it.  Quite ominous.  But the saturation could have been brought out a bit to make it more powerful.</td>', 'this sign is scary.  i like the REPENT!!! feel of it.  Quite ominous.  But the saturation could have been brought out a bit to make it more powerful.', '2005-02-02 13:36:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1146891, 142459, 31440, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot, just that the sign doesn''t add anything, or say anything really</td>', 'Beautiful shot, just that the sign doesn''t add anything, or say anything really', '2005-02-02 13:36:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1146895, 142251, 31865, '<td valign="top">This is pretty funny!  I would have liked it better if the sign was more to the left and you could see the outhouse a little better (but that tree would be in the way then).  The first time I looked at this, i didn''t notice the outhouse was there because the sign is the center of attention.  If there was some way to make that stand out a little more, maybe.  However, the subtlety is nice too.</td>', 'This is pretty funny!  I would have liked it better if the sign was more to the left and you could see the outhouse a little better (but that tree would be in the way then).  The first time I looked at this, i didn''t notice the outhouse was there because the sign is the center of attention.  If there was some way to make that stand out a little more, maybe.  However, the subtlety is nice too.', '2005-02-02 13:39:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1146896, 141144, 32513, '<td valign="top">From the looks of the sign, you must have used a direct fill flash. Even if its diffused, any direct flash on a sign like that is going to cause the sign to burn up and become white because the light goes straight back into the lens, it''s just like red eye, only in this case its with a sign. I''d suggest unmounting your flash and maybe lighting the sign from an extreme angle, so long as the light doesn''t go straight back into the lens, you should be ok, or at least better off. Over all, I like this photo, but it would be even better if the sign hadn''t burned up so badly. Nice job with the frame.</td>', 'From the looks of the sign, you must have used a direct fill flash. Even if its diffused, any direct flash on a sign like that is going to cause the sign to burn up and become white because the light goes straight back into the lens, it''s just like red eye, only in this case its with a sign. I''d suggest unmounting your flash and maybe lighting the sign from an extreme angle, so long as the light doesn''t go straight back into the lens, you should be ok, or at least better off. Over all, I like this photo, but it would be even better if the sign hadn''t burned up so badly. Nice job with the frame.', '2005-02-02 13:41:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1146898, 141629, 31440, '<td valign="top">The sign detracts from the picture, but would be a great tourist shot to show you''d been there...</td>', 'The sign detracts from the picture, but would be a great tourist shot to show you''d been there...', '2005-02-02 13:42:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1146899, 142108, 31865, '<td valign="top">the technique is interesting (was it done by zooming out on a long exposure?) but i don''t see how it relates to what the sign says.  If the sign said something like "watch for falling tress" that would have been more apt. Not bad though.</td>', 'the technique is interesting (was it done by zooming out on a long exposure?) but i don''t see how it relates to what the sign says.  If the sign said something like "watch for falling tress" that would have been more apt. Not bad though.', '2005-02-02 13:42:34.000000', NULL, 1),
