(1160606, 140883, 32147, '<td valign="top">I wanted to take a minute to thank everyone for their comments during this challenge.  I was very happy with the results from this photo.<br/> <br/>My goal for this shot was to de-emphasize the crossbuck, yet have it as an important element to the composition.  I was able to get the DOF very shallow by using a big lens:  a 170-500mm at about 175mm.  With this lens, I have to be very careful about focus, but fortunately it worked a treat this time.<br/> <br/>Thank you all again for your comments and suggestions.<br/> <br/>-Matthew-</td>', 'I wanted to take a minute to thank everyone for their comments during this challenge.  I was very happy with the results from this photo. My goal for this shot was to de-emphasize the crossbuck, yet have it as an important element to the composition.  I was able to get the DOF very shallow by using a big lens:  a 170-500mm at about 175mm.  With this lens, I have to be very careful about focus, but fortunately it worked a treat this time. Thank you all again for your comments and suggestions. -Matthew-', '2005-02-09 19:09:19.000000', NULL, 0),
