(1161452, 142184, 30584, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Puppies:</b></div><hr/><i> conveys a sense of oppression, like beyond is death. Interesting, certainly. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I just wanted to say that this post just tickled me..we live on an army base, and this sign is just on the gate, and beyond is the "bad" part of town off-base. so basically, beyond is death, hehe! also, those arent powerlines in the background, its actually razorwire that tops the fence the sign is on. Thanks for all the great comments!<br/>**edited for spelling<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-10 08:42:27.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Puppies: conveys a sense of oppression, like beyond is death. Interesting, certainly.  I just wanted to say that this post just tickled me..we live on an army base, and this sign is just on the gate, and beyond is the "bad" part of town off-base. so basically, beyond is death, hehe! also, those arent powerlines in the background, its actually razorwire that tops the fence the sign is on. Thanks for all the great comments!**edited for spelling', '2005-02-10 08:41:45.000000', '2005-02-10 08:42:27.000000', 0),
(1161674, 142434, 18868, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who voted, and an extra huge thanks to those who commented.  I''ll admit to some disapointment with the score, and the fine comments helped ease my mind.<br/> <br/>I understood the risk of entering an image that might be considered "religious" by voters.  I''m not a religious person, but Stacey was an active and respected member of his church, so it suits his memory.<br/> <br/>I guess that I was hoping to not be penalized for the image of a cross.  I was hoping that the voters could distinguish between a scene that contains a religious item and a scene that onerously promotes ones'' own religion, and just vote on the image.</td>', 'Thanks to all who voted, and an extra huge thanks to those who commented.  I''ll admit to some disapointment with the score, and the fine comments helped ease my mind. I understood the risk of entering an image that might be considered "religious" by voters.  I''m not a religious person, but Stacey was an active and respected member of his church, so it suits his memory. I guess that I was hoping to not be penalized for the image of a cross.  I was hoping that the voters could distinguish between a scene that contains a religious item and a scene that onerously promotes ones'' own religion, and just vote on the image.', '2005-02-10 12:49:50.000000', NULL, 0),
