(1162356, 141591, 20066, '<td valign="top">Thanks all.<br/>It is my second highest voting and my highest percentage so far.<br/>This photo is one of the few I have submitted that went higher than I expected.  But that''s nice with this one since I like it a lot now.<br/> <br/>The only bad thing is that it was above my "3" challenge entry which I think is much better.  And I still dont''t understand the low score for my faceless entry.<br/> <br/>About comments then I don''t understand what ergates means by saying "it would have  been better with a more careful composition" since it is the composition what I like in the photo.  That''s the reason his/her comment wasn''t considered helpful.<br/> <br/>And about that traffic sing.  It is actually there and at the vanishing point on the left side of the road you can see a farm and there is another one on the right side and children can be on the road while playing or visiting each other.<br/> <br/>And it is not completely somewhere in the middle of nowhere since it is almost inside Reykjavik if it isn''t inside the boundaries of the capital.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-10 19:27:59.</i></td>', 'Thanks all.It is my second highest voting and my highest percentage so far.This photo is one of the few I have submitted that went higher than I expected.  But that''s nice with this one since I like it a lot now. The only bad thing is that it was above my "3" challenge entry which I think is much better.  And I still dont''t understand the low score for my faceless entry. About comments then I don''t understand what ergates means by saying "it would have  been better with a more careful composition" since it is the composition what I like in the photo.  That''s the reason his/her comment wasn''t considered helpful. And about that traffic sing.  It is actually there and at the vanishing point on the left side of the road you can see a farm and there is another one on the right side and children can be on the road while playing or visiting each other. And it is not completely somewhere in the middle of nowhere since it is almost inside Reykjavik if it isn''t inside the boundaries of the capital.', '2005-02-10 19:26:08.000000', '2005-02-10 19:27:59.000000', 0),
