(2095104, 142676, 27164, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mandyturner:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice composition, little noisy. I don''t understand your title? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>For the title, I was referring to the time in the Catholic Church in which there were two Popes (1378-1417) where one sat in Avignon and the other sat in Rome.  A time of division, really.</td>', 'Originally posted by mandyturner: Nice composition, little noisy. I don''t understand your title?  For the title, I was referring to the time in the Catholic Church in which there were two Popes (1378-1417) where one sat in Avignon and the other sat in Rome.  A time of division, really.', '2006-01-28 11:31:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2227696, 140670, 16912, '<td valign="top">My work is done here (for now) my 10th comment on your work tonight Rex and I find I''ve voted on this in the challenge (didn''t comment however). <br/> <br/>I gave it a 5. As other commenters mentioned, its not an image that makes you go ''wow'' and although I''m happy with the composition ''middle of the road'' is the best I can come up with. Oh, if you drive this way to work everyday I''m a little worried you didn''t know you were entering a 25mph zone!!</td>', 'My work is done here (for now) my 10th comment on your work tonight Rex and I find I''ve voted on this in the challenge (didn''t comment however).  I gave it a 5. As other commenters mentioned, its not an image that makes you go ''wow'' and although I''m happy with the composition ''middle of the road'' is the best I can come up with. Oh, if you drive this way to work everyday I''m a little worried you didn''t know you were entering a 25mph zone!!', '2006-03-14 17:02:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2296504, 142205, 56776, '<td valign="top">Loved this!!  When I was a girl of 6 or 7, my parents and I were travelling in Maine and saw an almost identical sign.  That was in the mid-50s.  The sign and our amused reation to it became part of our family lore over the years.  -- Barbara Concord, MA</td>', 'Loved this!!  When I was a girl of 6 or 7, my parents and I were travelling in Maine and saw an almost identical sign.  That was in the mid-50s.  The sign and our amused reation to it became part of our family lore over the years.  -- Barbara Concord, MA', '2006-04-07 23:35:46.000000', NULL, 0),
